anningTree(weight:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Prim’s algorithm over every component (NetworkX, JGraphT, igraph): grows a tree from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first unspanned vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, joining the lightest edge out of it each step,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and repeats until every vertex is spanned. A minimum spanning forest; among equal weights,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which edges it chooses is unspecified (a canonical choice is measurably slower; see the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"benchmarks). Edges are listed in the order their far vertices joined, so each joins a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spanned vertex to a new one; the weight is added up in that order."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/primMinimumSpanningTree(weight:)","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/primminimumspanningtree(weight:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"primMinimumSpanningTree(weight:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"primMinimumSpanningTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpanningForest","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier